# Android local build + publish (Windows)

Hiago forbade EAS / Expo cloud. Compile release with Gradle on this PC, then put the APK on the download page via GitHub release + Coolify. Full agent playbook: `CLAUDE.md` → **Como publicar (APK + VPS)**.

## Trees

| Role | Path |
| --- | --- |
| Edit / git | OneDrive `…\Égua, adota!` |
| Compile | `C:\dev\egua-adota` (preferred: has `android/` + hoisted `node_modules`). Fallback short tree: `C:\egua`. |

Windows `CMAKE_OBJECT_PATH_MAX` is 250. Building from a long Desktop/OneDrive path breaks ninja. `subst` does not help. Never `/MIR` robocopy. Never copy `node_modules`. Do not commit `apps/mobile/android` (CNG, gitignored).

## pnpm

Root `packageManager: pnpm@9.15.9`. pnpm 10 cannot install this lockfile. `.npmrc` has `node-linker=hoisted`. Do not run a full `pnpm install` on every ship — only rebuild `@patinha/shared` if `dist` was wiped by robocopy.

## Sync before Gradle

1. Robocopy edit tree → compile tree `/E`, exclude `android`, `node_modules`, `.expo`, `.git`, `.env`.
2. `node apps/mobile/scripts/bump-build.mjs --sync` so `android/app/build.gradle` `versionCode` matches `version.json`.
3. Keep `apps/mobile/.env` on the compile tree (do not commit):

- `EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://adota-api.warlord-core.site`
- `EXPO_PUBLIC_DOWNLOAD_URL=https://adota.warlord-core.site`

## Gradle

- Open / build under `…\apps\mobile\android`, not the monorepo root.
- JDK **17** only. On this PC `org.gradle.java.home` points at Adoptium under `C:\Users\hiago\.gradle\jdks\…` (gitignored). Studio JBR 25 breaks Prefab/worklets.
- Node: `C:\nvm4w\nodejs`. From `apps\mobile`, `require.resolve('react-native/package.json')` must resolve to the **hoisted** root `node_modules`.
- SDK: `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Android\Sdk`. NDK `27.1.12297006`. Manifest needs `usesCleartextTraffic=true` (HTTP test API).
- Release signing = debug keystore (Expo template). Uninstall old debug app if install fails.
- **assembleRelease**, not debug. Quote `-PreactNativeArchitectures=arm64-v8a` in PowerShell.
- Set `NODE_ENV=production` for the Gradle process (`NODE_ENV=test` from vitest breaks the release JS bundle). Prefer `GRADLE_USER_HOME=C:\Users\hiago\.gradle` and `TEMP`/`TMP=C:\Temp`.

Expected APK: `apps\mobile\android\app\build\outputs\apk\release\app-release.apk` (~80–90 MB). A ~287 MB debug APK that asks for a Metro URL is wrong.

## After the APK

1. Commit + push `master` with bumped `version.json`, `download/version.json`, and `docker/download.Dockerfile` `APK_URL` pointing at the new tag.
2. GitHub release tag `apk-<version>-<build>`, asset filename **`egua-adota.apk`**. `gh` is not installed — use `git credential fill` + a temp Node script under `C:\Temp`; never print the token; delete the script after.
3. Coolify Deploy on app `fpmewu0com3qkbfihrsihc6y` (header Deploy button, not the sidebar expander). Panel host: `painel.warlord-core.site`. Do not touch MetalRiff, chatbot, teste-AtivaFacil; do not Cancel / Danger Zone / Coolify upgrade.
4. Confirm live `https://download-…/version.json` has the new `androidVersionCode` before telling Hiago to reopen the app.

Volume-only APK copies are wiped by `docker/download-entrypoint.sh` on every start. Durable path = GitHub release + Dockerfile `APK_URL` + Coolify rebuild.

